EXAMPLE a RECORD prints its parser and its formatter in the order of its fields
  SOURCE RECORD sync_ack SyncAck LEAD sync_ack
  SOURCE   FIELD epoch int
  SOURCE   FIELD will_compile bool
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pyrecord class SyncAck(NamedTuple):
  EXPECT rendered.pyrecord ("will_compile", "bool"),
  EXPECT rendered.pyrecord ), head="sync_ack")
  EXPECT rendered.csrecord internal static string FormatSyncAck(
  EXPECT rendered.csrecord sb.Append("sync_ack");

EXAMPLE an OPTIONAL field is nullable in Python and skipped by the C# formatter when null
  SOURCE RECORD sync_status SyncStatus
  SOURCE   FIELD epoch int
  SOURCE   FIELD err text OPTIONAL
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT rendered.pyrecord err: text | None = None
  EXPECT rendered.csrecord text_opt err= default,
  EXPECT rendered.csrecord if (err != null) sb.Append(sb.Length == 0 ? "" : "|").Append("err=").Append(Wire.w_text(err));
  EXPECT unrendered.pyrecord head=

EXAMPLE a lower-case class name is refused
  SOURCE RECORD x xClass
  SOURCE   FIELD a int
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:10

EXAMPLE a field type outside the list and a duplicate field are refused
  SOURCE RECORD x X
  SOURCE   FIELD a integer
  SOURCE   FIELD b int
  SOURCE   FIELD b int
  SOURCE END
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:11
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_DUPLICATE at 4:9
